      "content": "1. Circulatory System – Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Blood is a fluid connective tissue consisting of 55% liquid plasma and 45% formed elements (RBCs, WBCs, and Platelets).",
        "Red Blood Cells contain hemoglobin for oxygen transport, lack a nucleus at maturity, and are destroyed in the spleen.",
        "The human heart is a four-chambered muscular organ that maintains double circulation to separate oxygenated and deoxygenated blood.",
        "The lymphatic system drains excess tissue fluid back into the vascular system and plays a vital role in immune defense."
      ],
